==Trivia==
*Though treated as the first of the standard Uber sets, it is technically the sixth, as it wasn't until [[Version 3.4 Update|Version 3.4]] with the release of Asiluga through Balaluga that it became its own banner. Before then, Nekoluga was part of the general Rare Gacha pool.
**This could still be seen in [[The Battle Cats POP!]], which only had content from up to [[Version 2.7 Update|Version 2.7]] of [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]].
*The Lugas are cat-abominations, each with a different trait that makes them unique, which is mentioned in their respective description. Their weirdness comes from a bony body with some parts stretched, different in each member. Kesalan has a long build overall, Asilan has long legs, Kubilan has a long neck, Tesalan has long arms, Balalan has his limbs separated, Togelan has many spikes, Nobilan has a curly body, Papalan looks like Kesalan, but very old and fragile, Furilan has very long hair, Kaolan has a very big head, and Mamolan is mostly composed of a torso.
*Most of their names are taken from words related to what part of them is abnormal in their evolved form (some already seen on their normal form)
**Neko-luga; taken from ネコ/neko/cat to connect the whole family to Battle Cats
**Asi-luga; taken from 脚/ashi/leg
**Kubi-luga; taken from 首/kubi/neck
**Te-coluga; taken from 手/te/hand
**Bala-luga; taken from ばらばら/bara bara/scattered or 腹/hara/stomach
**Toge-luga; taken from 棘/toge/spike
**Nobi-luga; taken from のびる/nobiru/stretches
**Papa-luga; taken from papa/father (in Japanese, Oi-luga; taken from 老いる/oiru/aging)
**Furi-luga; taken from fury (in Japanese, Oko-luga; taken from 怒る/okoru/angry)
**Kao-luga; taken from 顔/kao/face
**Mamo-luga; taken from 守る/mamoru/to protect
**Lege-luga; taken from legend
**Mimi-luga; taken from 耳/mimi/ear
*All of their True Forms reference some kind of popular Japanese media, mostly shows or manga/anime.
**Ultralan Pasalan's references [[wikipedia:Ultraman (character)|Ultraman]], the main character of the [[wikipedia:Ultraman|eponymous show]].
**Assassinlan Pasalan is a reference to [[wikipedia:Kenshiro|Kenshiro]] from the anime ''[[wikipedia:Fist of the North Star|Fist of the North Star]]''.
**E. Kubilan Pasalan is based on [[E. Honda (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Honda]] from the fighting game series ''[[wikipedia:Street Fighter|Street Fighter]]''.
**Lufalan Pasalan is based on [[wikia:one-piece:Monkey D. Luffy|Monkey D. Luffy]] from the manga/anime ''[[wikipedia:One Piece|One Piece]]''.
**Piccolan Pasalan resembles the Angel [[The 4th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|Sachiel]] from the anime ''[[wikipedia:Neon Genesis Evangelion|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]''.
**Shishilan Pasalan resembles the [[wikia:ghibli:Forest Spirit|Night Walker]] from the movie ''[[wikipedia:Princess Mononoke|Princess Mononoke]],'' also known as a ''Shishigami''.
**Mystican Pasalan is a reference to the [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Hero_(Dragon_Quest_V) main protagonist] from the role playing game ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest V|Dragon Quest V]]'', and also resembles [[wikia:hunterxhunter:Ging Freecss|Ging Freecss]] from the anime ''[[wikipedia:Hunter × Hunter|Hunter × Hunter]]''.
**Sukelan Kakulan resembles Mitsuemon, the false identity of Tokugawa Mitsukuni in the long-running period drama ''[[wikipedia:Mito Kōmon|Mito Kōmon]]''.
**Ragelan Pasalan resembles [[wikia:hunterxhunter:Gon|Gon Freecss]] from ''Hunter x Hunter'' in his temporary aged and furious form.
*If the player enters the Rare Cat Capsule in an outdated version of the game, this is the only available Uber Rare set (unless all Lugas are not added in that update yet, the same for other Uber Rare sets)
*All Ubers in this set share a cost of 4,500¢, with the exception of Nobiluga's true form, Mystican Pasalan, who costs 2,250¢.
*Older versions of this set's poster referred to Togelan Pasalan as "she", despite its descriptions having always referred to it as a "he".
*Pasalan, being the phrase that every Uber Rare in this set has, is a reference to an Edo Period folklore about a mysterious creature, Kesaran Pasalan, a white and fluffy youkai/fictional cryptid that brings good luck and happiness to the place it is in.

